.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-claim-check 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-claim\-check \- Refuse a pull of an issue somebody is already on, and mint the receipt when it is free
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten claim check\fR [\fB\-\-takeover\fR] [\fB\-\-bypass\-sequence\fR] [\fB\-\-adopt\fR] [\fB\-\-adopt\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Refuse a pull of an issue somebody is already on, and mint the receipt when it is free
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-takeover\fR
Claim over the competitor refusals, recording in the receipt which ones were overridden
.TP
\fB\-\-bypass\-sequence\fR
Skip the refinement\-sequence rules, recorded in the receipt as a bypass
.TP
\fB\-\-adopt\fR
Re\-key an orphaned claim receipt onto this branch instead of judging a payload
.TP
\fB\-\-adopt\-from\fR
The branch name the receipt being adopted was minted under
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\fR
Resolve the payload from the capture store by this issue key instead of reading stdin
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
